      "latency_ms": 2263.2,
      "prompt_tokens": 11,
      "completion_tokens": 540,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical compound made up of two elements: **hydrogen and oxygen**. Its chemical formula is **$\\text{H}_2\\text{O}$**, meaning each molecule consists of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom. \n\nHowever, to humans, Earth, and all known life, water is much more than just a chemical formula. Here is a breakdown of what water is through different lenses:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Physical Substance\nWater is unique because it is the only natural substance on Earth that exists abundantly in three physical states:\n*   **Liquid:** The oceans, rivers, and rain we see every day.\n*   **Solid (Ice):** Glaciers, snow, and ice cubes.\n*   **Gas (Vapor):** Steam, humidity, and clouds in the atmosphere.\n\nAt standard temperature and pressure, liquid water is transparent, odorless, and tasteless. \n\n### 2. The \"Universal Solvent\"\nWater has a unique chemical structure (it is a \"polar\" molecule, meaning the oxygen side has a slight negative charge and the hydrogen side has a slight positive charge). Because of this, water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This is why it is called the **universal solvent**. \n*   It dissolves salt, sugar, minerals, and nutrients, allowing living things to absorb essential chemicals.\n\n### 3. The Essence of Life\nWater is the fundamental building block of all known life. \n*   **Inside living things:** The human body is made of about 60% water. Water regulates body temperature, lubricates joints, flushes out waste, and transports nutrients through the blood.\n*   **Evolution:** Life itself is believed to have originated in Earth's primordial oceans.\n\n### 4. Earth’s Life Support System\nOften called the **\"Blue Planet,\"** Earth’s surface is about 71% water, with the vast majority of it contained in the oceans (about 96.5% of which is salt water). \n*   **The Water Cycle:** Water is constantly recycled through evaporation, condensation, and precipitation (rain and snow). The water you drink today is the exact same water that dinosaurs drank millions of years ago.\n*   **Climate Regulator:** Oceans absorb and redistribute massive amounts of heat from the sun, stabilizing the Earth’s climate and weather patterns.\n\n### Summary\nWater is the ultimate connector on our planet. It shapes our geography, drives our weather, constitutes our bodies, and enables every chemical reaction necessary for life to exist."
